# Auracle API

## Overview

The Auracle API provides both REST and WebSocket interfaces for interacting with our services. The REST API follows standard HTTP conventions and supports both Prime and Sovereign tiers, while the WebSocket API enables real-time data exchange.

# REST API

## Base URL

All REST API endpoints are prefixed with `/v1/`. For example:
- Production: `https://api.auracle.digital/v1/`
- Test: `https://test-api.auracle.digital/v1/`

## Authentication

### Login with API Key

```http
POST /v1/auth/login
```

Request:
```json
{
    "apiKey": "your_api_key",
    "apiSecret": "your_api_secret"
}
```

Response:
```json
{
    "token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...",
    "expiresAt": "2024-03-20T12:00:00Z"
}
```

### API Key Management

#### List API Keys
```http
GET /v1/auth/keys
```

Response:
```json
{
    "keys": [
        {
            "id": "key_123",
            "name": "Production Key",
            "createdAt": "2024-03-01T00:00:00Z",
            "lastUsed": "2024-03-19T15:30:00Z"
        }
    ]
}
```

#### Generate New API Key
```http
POST /v1/auth/keys
```

Request:
```json
{
    "name": "New API Key",
    "permissions": ["read", "write"]
}
```

Response:
```json
{
    "id": "key_456",
    "apiKey": "ak_live_...",
    "apiSecret": "as_live_...",
    "createdAt": "2024-03-19T16:00:00Z"
}
```

#### Revoke API Key
```http
DELETE /v1/auth/keys/{keyId}
```

## Health & Metrics

### Health Check
```http
GET /health
```

Response:
```json
{
    "status": "ok",
    "uptime": 1234567
}
```

### Metrics
```http
GET /metrics
```

Returns Prometheus-compatible metrics.

## Rate Limiting

Standard rate limit headers are included in all responses:
- `X-RateLimit-Limit`: Maximum requests per window
- `X-RateLimit-Remaining`: Remaining requests in current window
- `X-RateLimit-Reset`: Time when the rate limit resets

## Data Feeds

### Latest Aggregated Data
```http
GET /v1/feeds/{feedId}/latest
```

Response:
```json
{
    "feedId": "BTC-USD",
    "value": 65432.10,
    "timestamp": "2024-03-19T16:00:00Z",
    "confidence": 0.99
}
```

### Historical Data
```http
GET /v1/feeds/{feedId}/history?start=2024-03-01T00:00:00Z&end=2024-03-19T00:00:00Z&limit=100
```

Response:
```json
{
    "feedId": "BTC-USD",
    "data": [
        {
            "value": 65432.10,
            "timestamp": "2024-03-19T16:00:00Z"
        }
    ]
}
```

## Real-Time Streaming

### WebSocket Connection
```http
WebSocket /v1/stream
```

Subscribe message:
```json
{
    "action": "subscribe",
    "feeds": ["BTC-USD", "ETH-USD"]
}
```

Stream message:
```json
{
    "feedId": "BTC-USD",
    "value": 65432.10,
    "timestamp": "2024-03-19T16:00:00Z"
}
```

## Verifiable Randomness (VRF)

### Request Randomness
```http
POST /v1/vrf/requests
```

Request:
```json
{
    "consumerId": "my-app",
    "numWords": 1,
    "confirmationCount": 3,
    "callbackUrl": "https://my-app.com/vrf-callback"
}
```

Response:
```json
{
    "requestId": "vrf_123",
    "status": "pending",
    "requestedAt": "2024-03-19T16:00:00Z"
}
```

### Check Request Status
```http
GET /v1/vrf/requests/{requestId}
```

Response:
```json
{
    "requestId": "vrf_123",
    "status": "fulfilled",
    "randomWords": ["0x1234..."],
    "proof": "0x5678...",
    "fulfilledAt": "2024-03-19T16:01:00Z"
}
```

## Error Handling

All errors follow this format:
```json
{
    "code": "INVALID_REQUEST",
    "message": "Invalid request parameters",
    "details": {
        "field": "amount",
        "reason": "must be positive"
    }
}
```

Common error codes:
- 400: Bad Request
- 401: Unauthorized
- 403: Forbidden
- 404: Not Found
- 429: Too Many Requests
- 500: Internal Server Error

# WebSocket API

## Overview

The Auracle API employs WebSockets for communication between the front-end and back-end services, allowing real-time data exchange. For developers aiming to programmatically interact with Auracle, a direct WebSocket connection to the back-end service can be established.

Please note, this API was initially designed for internal use, primarily for front-end development. Therefore, it may possess some complex payloads. Furthermore, it is subject to potential changes based on the evolving needs of the front-end application.

# Connection Details

## Base URL

Assuming your Auracle URL is https://test.auracle.digital/, your corresponding WebSocket URL would be: wss://test-backend.auracle.digital/v1.

The backend service adheres to the same IP whitelist policies as the front-end service. If you need to add (static) IP addresses to the whitelist, please contact our support team.

## Pricing
## JSON-RPC Schema


| Name   | Type   | Description |
--------|--------|-------------
|jsonrpc | string | Only "2.0" is supported |
|id      | string | This will be echoed back in responses or subscription payloads|
|method  | string | Establishing the specific API to connect to. Documented below |
|params  | string | Details regarding the specific API call. Documented below     |

# Authentication

After you've established a WebSocket connection, you will need to authenticate before you can call the other methods.

## Login

First of all, you will need to log in with your Access credentials. In return, you will receive a token.



```json
{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": "9cc9e382-ba9a-4992-80aa-fc77628a15d9",
    "method": "login",
    "params": {
        "username": "YOUR_USERNAME",
        "password": "YOUR_PASSWORD"
    }
}
```

### Request

Name | Type | Description
--------- | ------- | -----------
username | string | Access username
password | string | Corresponding password

```json
{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": "9cc9e382-ba9a-4992-80aa-fc77628a15d9",
    "result": {
        "token": "YOUR_TOKEN"
    }
}
```
### Response

Name | Type | Description
--------- | ------- | -----------
token | string | Authentication token to be used later

## authenticate_with_token

You will need to pass the token from the previous step to this method. Once you have received a positive confirmation, your WebSocket connection is authenticated.



```json
{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": "6dce2124-20b7-4eac-bb94-960539f027f0",
    "method": "authenticate_with_token",
    "params": {
        "auth_token": "YOUR_TOKEN"
    }
}
```

### Request

Name | Type | Description
--------- | ------- | -----------
auth_token | string | Authentication Token received from login



```json
{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": "6dce2124-20b7-4eac-bb94-960539f027f0",
    "result": "ok"
}
```
### Response

Name | Type | Description
--------- | ------- | -----------
result | string | Confirmation of request. "ok" indicates positive confirmation.  <br /> Negative confirmation will display an "error" field instead of "result"

